  "query_preview": "..\nNewly-formed Invest 93W is a very weak embedded monsoon disturbance\nwell west of the Marianas, which is expected to induce low-end\nscattered showers tonight. Mostly dry conditions will return \nthereafter as winds remain light, followed by a monsoon surge \ndeveloping across the region beginning this weekend. Said monsoon\nsurge will introduce southwesterly to westerly winds and a wet \npattern coming into next week, with winds likely to keep increasing\nas Typhoon Dolphin (12W) moves between the far northern CNMI and \nWake Island.",
